  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Booz Allen Hamilton obligated $5.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Booz Allen Hamilton won 959 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $5.9M. Obligations are down 13.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a multi-year record with FY21 at $5.1B, FY22 at $5.6B, FY23 at $6.5B, FY24 at $7.1B, FY25 at $6.6B, and FY26 at $5.7B. General Services Administration is the largest buying agency in FY2026 to date at $2.5B, followed by Department of Defense at $1.8B and Department of Health and Human Services at $388M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market by NAICS at $1.7B, followed by Engineering Services at $1.4B and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $731M. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date contract obligations, while some largest-awards and expiring-contracts values are total contract values rather than obligations. This profile highlights where Booz Allen Hamilton’s federal revenue is concentrated by agency and market for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Booz Allen Hamilton’s biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "General Services Administration is the biggest buyer of Booz Allen Hamilton in FY2026 to date at $2.5B. Department of Defense is the next largest buyer at $1.8B. Department of Health and Human Services, Department of Veterans Affairs, and Department of Homeland Security follow with $388M, $293M, and $122M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets drive Booz Allen Hamilton’s federal work?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for Booz Allen Hamilton at $1.7B, and Engineering Services is the second largest at $1.4B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services contribute $731M and $685M respectively. Custom Computer Programming Services, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services, and other listed NAICS fill out the remaining federal portfolio."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Booz Allen Hamilton make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Booz Allen Hamilton obligated $5.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Booz Allen Hamilton’s fiscal-year obligations have ranged from $5.1B in FY21 up to $7.1B in FY24, with FY25 at $6.6B and the current FY26 total at $5.7B. The company won 959 awards this fiscal year and the average award size is $5.9M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Booz Allen Hamilton?",
      "a": "General Services Administration, Department of Defense, and Department of Health and Human Services are the top buyers of Booz Allen Hamilton in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration obligated $2.5B, Department of Defense obligated $1.8B, and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $388M. Other federal buyers include Department of Veterans Affairs at $293M and Department of Homeland Security at $122M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Booz Allen Hamilton sell to the government?",
      "a": "Computer Systems Design Services, Engineering Services, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) are the primary markets for Booz Allen Hamilton. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $1.7B, Engineering Services accounts for $1.4B, and that R&D category accounts for $731M. Additional markets include All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $685M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $483M."
    },
